<title>USA: INTERPUBLIC UNIT BUYS NEW YORK AD AGENCY.</title>
<headline>INTERPUBLIC UNIT BUYS NEW YORK AD AGENCY.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interpublic Group of Cos Inc's DrafDirect Worldwide said Wednesday it bought New York advertising agency Adler, Boschetto Peebles &amp; Partners for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>The direct marketing firm said the ad agency has annual billing of $135 million and employs 114.</p>
<p>Company officials were not immediately available to elaborate on the deal.</p>
